{#- The six menu items from the briefing's page table. Contact is an anchor to a
    section on the homepage, not a page of its own — section 5 of the briefing.
    Kept inline rather than in _data/nav.json: it is one short list, edited by us
    and never by Sarah, and a second file would only spread it out. -#}
{% set navItems = [
  { label: "Home",                href: "/" },
  { label: "Testimonials",        href: "/testimonials/" },
  { label: "Fees",                href: "/fees/" },
  { label: "Book a consultation", href: "/book/" },
  { label: "Blog",                href: "/blog/" },
  { label: "Contact",             href: "/#contact" }
] %}

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="site-header__bar">

    {#- aria-hidden on the mark so the link reads "Sarah Philip", not "SP Sarah Philip".
        The design has CV / Career CV here; SP / Sarah Philip is the briefing's working
        name and your instruction. -#}
    <a class="site-brand" href="/">
      <span class="site-brand__mark" aria-hidden="true">SP</span>
      <span class="site-brand__name">Sarah Philip</span>
    </a>

    {#- A real button, so Enter and Space both activate it with no key handling of
        our own, and it is in the tab order for free. type="button" because the
        default is submit.

        aria-expanded is the attribute a screen reader announces as collapsed or
        expanded, and base.css keys the panel off that same attribute — one piece
        of state, so the announcement and the visible panel cannot disagree.

        The label stays "Menu" when open. aria-expanded already carries the state;
        renaming the control to "Close" mid-interaction changes its identity under
        someone who is listening to it. -#}
    <button type="button" class="menu-toggle"
            aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="site-nav" aria-label="Menu">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </button>

  </div>

  {#- Sibling of the bar rather than inside it, so the panel spans the full width
      below the header row. -#}
  <nav id="site-nav" class="site-nav">
    <ul class="site-nav__list">
      {%- for item in navItems %}
      <li><a href="{{ item.href }}"{% if item.href == page.url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>

</header>
